# Dual-platform + bilingual strings

WeatherTrip is a monorepo: `apps/web` (Next.js), `apps/mobile` (Expo), shared copy in `packages/i18n`.

## Required on every product change

1. **English and Finnish** — edit `packages/i18n/src/en.ts` and `packages/i18n/src/fi.ts` together. Same keys in both; never leave FI (or EN) missing.
2. **Web and Expo** — implement user-facing features in both apps unless the change is inherently platform-only (document why if skipped).
3. **No local-only dictionaries** — do not add strings only under `apps/web/src/i18n` or hardcode mobile UI text; use `@weathertrip/i18n`.

## Quick checklist

- [ ] New/changed key in `en.ts`
- [ ] Matching key in `fi.ts`
- [ ] Web UI updated (`apps/web`)
- [ ] Mobile UI updated (`apps/mobile`) when the feature applies
- [ ] API changes stay compatible for mobile (`EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL` clients)
